This is a tracked write, not a read-only query, so the entity has to be loaded and tracked. I used query syntax, a `var` assigned separately from the awaited execution, and the `CancellationToken`.

```csharp
public async Task RenamePostAsync(BlogContext context, int postId, string newTitle, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
{
    var postQuery =
        from post in context.Posts
        where post.Id == postId
        select post;

    var matchingPost = await postQuery.SingleOrDefaultAsync(cancellationToken);

    if (matchingPost == null)
    {
        throw new KeyNotFoundException($"Post {postId} was not found.");
    }

    matchingPost.Title = newTitle;
    await context.SaveChangesAsync(cancellationToken);
}
```

